  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-kit",
      "text": "`dsh-context-kit` is one DeepSeek Harness bundle that installs native context-management and history-editing features:"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-kit",
      "text": "- **DCP** adds model-directed compression and deterministic context cleanup.\n- **Context Mode** adds sandboxed processing and a searchable local knowledge base so large outputs do not have to enter the conversation.\n- **History Editor** edits user messages and the effective assistant text used by later turns.\n- **CDSH** is shipped as a nested package and mounted by the same bundle."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-kit",
      "text": "The bundle reimplements useful behavior in Harness-native services. It does not copy the upstream DCP or context-mode source."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js 22.19 or newer.\n- A compatible DeepSeek Harness installation that supplies the optional `@deepseek-ai/*` peer packages declared in `package.json`.\n- The Harness `plugin_manager` tool.\n\nMIT licensed. Installation from the Git checkout is supported; no registry publication is required."
    },
    {
      "section": "Supported installation",
      "text": "Install the repository as a bundle. Do not copy files into a profile, edit a profile manifest, create junctions, or run migration scripts."
    },
    {
      "section": "Local checkout",
      "text": "1. Clone or copy the repository to a normal workspace outside the DSH profile.\n2. Ask a Harness agent to call `plugin_manager` with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"install_bundle\",\n  \"target\": \"<absolute-path-to-the-checkout>\"\n}\n\nUse the repository root as `target`, not `lib`, `packages/cdsh`, or a generated archive."
    },
    {
      "section": "Git checkout",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/axtrask/dsh-context-kit.git dsh-context-kit\n```\n\nInstall that absolute checkout path with the same `plugin_manager install_bundle` call, or let the profile depend on the repository directly — the spec `pnpm add` accepts:\n\n```sh\npnpm add git+https://github.com/axtrask/dsh-context-kit.git\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Git checkout",
      "text": "For an update, pull the desired revision and install the same absolute checkout path again. Read the `application` and `warnings` fields returned by `plugin_manager`; they state whether the update was applied live or needs a restart."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installed composition",
      "text": "`cordis.patch.yml` inserts exactly two enabled Host rows:\n\n| Loader id | Package | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `context-kit-bundle` | `dsh-context-kit` | Aggregate DCP, Context Mode, and History Editor Host and Web client |\n| `cdsh` | `./packages/cdsh/lib/index.js` | Nested CDSH package shipped in this bundle |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installed composition",
      "text": "The Context Kit row is deliberately aggregate. Do not mount `dsh-context-kit/dcp-plugin`, `dsh-context-kit/context-mode-plugin`, or `dsh-context-kit/editor-plugin` as extra Loader rows: they would duplicate the owning package's Web client and service contributions."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings",
      "text": "The aggregate package owns one **Context Kit** scope in **Settings > Plugins**. Its values are grouped beneath three nested sections:\n\n- `dcp` — compression, pruning, protected tools, notifications, and subagent policy;\n- `contextMode` — capture limits, search limits, sandbox routing, and knowledge-base behavior;\n- `historyEditor` — Edit History availability and idle-session safety."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings",
      "text": "The default patch enables all three sections. DCP also enables `includeContextStatus`, matching the current supported runtime behavior.\n\nCDSH is a separate nested package in the same installation. Its Loader row is not another Context Kit settings namespace."
    },
    {
      "section": "Package contract",
      "text": "The publication root is `dsh-context-kit` version `0.1.11`:\n\n- `lib/` is the canonical implementation;\n- `locale/` contains package and component metadata;\n- `cordis.patch.yml` declares the two supported Loader rows;\n- `packages/cdsh/` is the only nested package;\n- `undici` is the only ordinary runtime dependency;\n- compatible Harness libraries are optional peers supplied by the installation and never\n  vendored into the checkout."
    },
    {
      "section": "Package contract",
      "text": "Development runtime generations are not part of the package. There are no `runtime`, `runtime-2`, or later cache-busting snapshots and no absolute machine paths in the packed files."
    },
    {
      "section": "Verification",
      "text": "From the repository root:\n\n```sh\nnpm run test:metadata\nnpm run test:edit-history\n```\n\n`test:metadata` validates the manifest, aggregate-plus-nested Loader topology, Web client identity, nested settings shape, and the `npm pack --dry-run` inventory. `test:edit-history` runs the five regression gates that protect the durable edit path, wire rewrite, Settings UI, and client load order.\n\nRun both groups with:\n\n```sh\nnpm run test:publication\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Verification",
      "text": "These tests inspect the checkout only. They do not install the bundle, modify a DSH profile, or restart a running Harness process."
    },
    {
      "section": "Main entry points",
      "text": "| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/index.js` | Aggregate Host entry exported by the package root |\n| `lib/plugin.js` | Shared Context Kit Host composition and nested config schema |\n| `lib/dcp.js` | DCP engine, compression tool, commands, and integration hooks |\n| `lib/context-mode.js` | Context Mode tools, routing guard, and knowledge-base integration |\n| `lib/edit-client.js` | Context Kit Settings card and Edit History Web integration |\n| `packages/cdsh/` | Nested CDSH package |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Main entry points",
      "text": "Legacy component exports remain available for programmatic compatibility, but the supported bundle composition mounts only the aggregate package root."
    }
  ],
